# TDE / DSA terminology

When writing UI labels, data fields, comments, docs, or translating German source material, use the **official English terms** from:

`TDE_DSA4_1_German_English_Abbreviations_and_Terminology.txt` (project root)

Consult that file for attributes, abbreviations, talents, advantages/disadvantages, weapons, and collision traps. Do not invent English names when the reference provides one.

## Critical abbreviation collisions

Never blindly translate these — German and English reuse the same letters:

| Letters | German rules | English rules |
|---------|--------------|---------------|
| TP | Trefferpunkte (weapon damage) | Talent Prowess (skill value) |
| SP | Schadenspunkte (damage after armor) | Spell Prowess (spell skill value) |
| ST | Silbertaler (currency) | Strength (attribute) |

## Project defaults (English UI)

- Attributes: CO, CL, IN, CH, DE, AG, CN, ST (not MU/KL/FF/GE/KO/KK)
- Vitality: VP (not LeP); Endurance: EP (not AuP); Magic: ASP (not AsP)
- Talent skill value: **TP**; spell skill value: **SP**
- Weapon damage before armor: **HP**; damage after armor: **DP**
- Armor: AR; encumbrance: EC / EEC; magic resistance: RM

When `german_name` is stored alongside an English `name`, keep the German original in data and show English in the UI per the reference file.
